WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.032
Some work shouldn't wait for a click. A weekly summary. A slow upload.

2
00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:05.577
Anything that takes a while.

3
00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:09.421
That's a background job. You describe it as steps, in order.

4
00:00:09.851 --> 00:00:16.622
Step one, collect the week's ideas. Done. Step two, write the summary.

5
00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:19.731
Done. Step three, save it. Done.

6
00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:23.327
Now run it again. Step one finishes. Step two fails.

7
00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:24.864
Maybe a service was busy.

8
00:00:25.294 --> 00:00:28.286
Without steps, you'd start over from the top.

9
00:00:28.316 --> 00:00:32.585
With steps, step one is already saved. Only step two runs again.

10
00:00:33.015 --> 00:00:37.258
It waits a moment, tries again, and this time it works.

11
00:00:37.288 --> 00:00:38.735
Step three follows.

12
00:00:39.165 --> 00:00:42.648
One more thing. A job runs when nobody's watching.

13
00:00:42.678 --> 00:00:45.177
So it has to tell you when it fails.

14
00:00:45.207 --> 00:00:48.269
If it can break silently, it isn't finished.
